cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use quantmet in published work, please cite it as below."
title: "quantmet: quantitative meteorology tools"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Corvec
    given-names: Shawn
repository-code: "https://github.com/scorvec/quantmet-tools"
url: "https://scorvec.com/quantmet-tools/"
license: MIT
version: "0.4.2"
date-released: "2026-10-15"
abstract: >-
  A Python toolkit for diagnosing atmospheric model output: transformed-Eulerian-mean and Eliassen-Palm
  diagnostics, downward control, the Takaya-Nakamura wave-activity flux, the Gill model, the QBO zero-wind line,
  Wheeler-Kiladis equatorial-wave filtering, Helmholtz decomposition, kinetic-energy spectra, potential vorticity and
  the dynamic tropopause, Rossby wave packets, tropical-cyclone diagnostics and detection, ensemble sensitivity,
  global conservation budgets, significance tests, forecast verification, moist thermodynamics and degree days.
keywords:
  - meteorology
  - atmospheric dynamics
  - stratosphere
  - Eliassen-Palm flux
  - transformed Eulerian mean
  - wave activity flux
  - equatorial waves
  - potential vorticity
  - tropical cyclones
  - forecast verification
  - thermodynamics
  - degree days
